This repository is licensed under the Taumorrow Demos License v3.1. The full text is the file `LICENSE` in the repository
taumorrow/tau-lang-demos at commit ff7edec6beca145a0146aa466f1fe3f51a640e06:
https://github.com/taumorrow/tau-lang-demos/blob/ff7edec6beca145a0146aa466f1fe3f51a640e06/LICENSE
That text, at that commit, is part of these terms. It applies here with the following readings, which take the place of the
parts of it that name the files and releases of tau-lang-demos:

1. Materials. In this repository, "Materials" means the file `PROVABLY_FAIR_GAMING_WHITEPAPER.MD` and every file added to
   this repository later that does not carry its own license text. This file (`LICENSE`) states the terms. The lists of
   Method, Tutorial and Classic Materials in section 1 of the full text, and its sentence on the archive, name files of
   tau-lang-demos; none of those files is in this repository. The Materials of this repository are Tutorial Materials in the
   sense of section 1 of the full text (the default class). The paper named in sections 0 and 4 of the full text is the
   paper with DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23163643. The file `PROVABLY_FAIR_GAMING_WHITEPAPER.MD` is an earlier account of the
   method by the same author and is a Material of this repository under these terms. The folder `the-round-as-a-formula/`
   and every file in it are not Materials; they are licensed under Creative Commons BY-NC-ND 4.0, as stated in
   `the-round-as-a-formula/LICENSE.md`.

2. What the Materials are (section 4 of the full text). The Materials of this repository are documents. They contain no
   specification files, no part specifications, no wiring table, no queries and no records. This license makes no
   statement that any system is fair, secure, or free of operator influence.

3. All other parts of the full text apply as written, including the definitions in section 1 (among them "Commercial Use"
   and "Tau-Net Ecosystem"), Tau Language and other works (section 2), the Method (section 3), the free grants (section 5),
   other Commercial Use and the agreement in section 8 (sections 7 and 8), what is not claimed and the patent paragraph
   (section 9), and the general terms (section 11).

4. Attribution (section 5 of the full text): keep this file with every copy or substantial portion of the Materials; its
   reference to the full text stands for "this license text". Credit "Taumorrow" in derived works, deployments and
   republications. Suggested wording: "based on work by Taumorrow (provably_fair_gaming)".

5. Earlier versions (in place of section 10, items 1 and 2, of the full text).
   - Releases of this repository before commit d51a050 remain under the license text each shipped with, if any; the last of them,
     commit 717b5c0, carried the "MIT License with Commercial Restriction for Provably Fair Gaming" (Copyright (c) 2025
     l0g1x).
   - Commit d51a050 (3 October 2026) carried the full text of the Taumorrow Demos License v3.0; that release remains under
     v3.0.
   - Commit b9e961b (5 October 2026) carried this text without the sentence on the folder `the-round-as-a-formula/` in
     item 1 and with item 2 worded for a repository of one document; that release remains under that wording.
   - Rights granted under those texts are not revoked by this one. If you obtained a release under an earlier license, that
     release stays under that license for you. Nothing here is retroactive.
   - Items 3 and 4 of section 10 of the full text apply: future releases may carry different terms, and each release
     carries its license in the `LICENSE` file at that commit. If you build on the Materials, pin a commit.

